{
  "id": "queue-kanji-shared-kanji",
  "title": "A kanji that the next words of a deck and of the deckless source both require is drawn by the first of them in source order, in the build and after every answer; no word is shown and then withdrawn (C-28d)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_shared_kanji"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "new_per_day is 5. The deck 'Words' (priority 0) holds the new kana word うっかり (card ...10) then the new word 日本語 (card ...20). The deckless source (scheduler.mined_priority default 0: the same tier) holds the new word 本 (card ...30), created before the kanji notes 本 (card ...40), 日 (card ...50) and 語 (card ...60), all new and deckless. Both 日本語 and the word 本 require the kanji 本.",
    "Step 0: the deck goes first on the tie: うっかり. The deckless source now has the fewest new cards (0 < 1) and its turn would draw [本 kanji, 本 word]; but the deck is earlier in source order and its next word 日本語 requires 本 too, so the deck takes the turn (QueueBuilder rule 4 'Turn order', step (c) 'earliest claimer'): 日, 本, 語, 日本語. That is 5 of 5; the word 本 does not fit. Order: うっかり, 日, 本, 語, 日本語. until_stop is 5.",
    "Step 1 answers うっかり Easy. Step 2: the same two steps of the rule give the tail of step 0: 日, 本, 語, 日本語. until_stop is 4.",
    "Steps 3-4 answer the kanji 日 and 本 Easy. Step 5: 本 is the last new card and the next words of both sources require it; the deck is first in source order (rule (a)), so the rest of its unit follows: 語, 日本語, the tail again. until_stop is 2. Picking the source with the fewest new cards here (the deckless source: its kanji cards do not count) would serve the word 本 instead, leave room for 語 only and withdraw 日本語 until the next day.",
    "Step 6, the next study day (04:00:01Z), 語 and 日本語 still new: the deck first on the tie, 語, 日本語; then the deckless word 本, whose kanji is started. until_stop is 3."
  ],
